#{[17592186400766 #edb/ref 1080 "$25$ and $9$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400766 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400766 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c56b5625-8f3f-5546-bd45-82c8dcf4f2c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400767 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\sqrt{7}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400767 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400767 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9f361d5f-db40-531a-8f20-5389f05b015d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400768 #edb/ref 1080 "$11$ and $7$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400768 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400768 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c82a5223-3bd0-5bad-9e6b-edd5899707f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400769 #edb/ref 1080 "$6$ and $4$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400769 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400769 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e7a6a4f9-ba6e-5a5b-9c4a-a88207909379" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400770 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400770 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400770 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400770 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/57/57368434b3025dc777c5be725da43e365dfd8ef3c47049570c0ecb13f2baf035.png)\n\nA $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ The corresponding ellipse and its principal axes are depicted in the diagram above. Given that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A,$ what are the nonzero singular values of $A?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400770 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f3e183c0-f2c5-57a2-8b6d-0c81e407e953" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400770 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix. Let \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\,…,{v}_{n}}\n$$\n\nbe an *orthonormal* basis of ${R}^{n}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=9={\\sigma }_{1},$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=4={\\sigma }_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the nonzero singular values of $A$ are ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186400772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e0b9d051-ab23-5d38-8461-85040e182756" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400772 #edb/ref 1080 "$9$ and $4$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400772 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400772 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47ade149-2321-54bc-8689-575d0021aa81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400773 #edb/ref 1080 "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400773 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400773 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0322f6ef-5cd8-5b08-95d5-f8a6bea015f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400774 #edb/ref 1080 "$9{v}_{1}$ and $4{v}_{1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400774 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400774 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56994b9b-ba0c-523d-9995-ad7e4cb025c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186